#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:88
msgid "Redirect and 404 management abilities provided by 404 to 301."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:136
msgid "List Redirects"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:137
msgid "Returns a page of redirect rules with their source, destination, status code, match type, hit count and whether they are enabled. Filterable by search term, match type, status code and enabled state."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:146
msgid "Match against the source and destination."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:154
msgid "HTTP status code the rule sends, e.g. 301."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:170
msgid "Create Redirect"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:171
msgid "Creates a redirect rule. The source is a path or pattern on this site; the destination is either a URL or the ID of an existing page. Rejects a source that duplicates an existing rule, an invalid regular expression, and a destination equal to its own source."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:188
msgid "Update Redirect"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:189
msgid "Updates an existing redirect rule. Only the fields passed in are changed; everything else is left as it is. Use this to repoint, re-code or disable a rule."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:197
#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:222
msgid "The redirect ID."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:214
msgid "Delete Redirect"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:215
msgid "Permanently deletes a redirect rule and unlinks it from any 404 log entry it was resolving. Disabling a rule is usually the safer option — see the update ability."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:243
msgid "Test a URL Against the Redirects"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:244
msgid "Resolves a path the way the plugin would for a real visitor and reports what happens: which rule matches (if any), the destination it sends them to, the status code, and whether the site-wide 404 fallback would take over instead. Changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:251
msgid "Path or URL to resolve, e.g. /old-post/."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:263
msgid "Which mechanism handles the request: a redirect rule, the site-wide 404 fallback, or nothing."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:267
msgid "Where the visitor lands; null when nothing redirects them."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:294
msgid "List 404 Logs"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:295
msgid "Returns a page of logged 404 requests with the requested path, referrer, hit count and whether the entry is still open. Sort by hits to find the URLs worth fixing first."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:304
msgid "Match against the requested path and the referrer."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:309
#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:360
msgid "0 open, 1 ignored, 2 fixed."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:324
msgid "Summarise 404 Logs"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:325
msgid "Returns how many logged 404s are open, ignored, fixed and resolved by a custom redirect. A cheap health check to run before listing anything."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:347
msgid "Update a 404 Log Entry"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:348
msgid "Marks a logged 404 as open, ignored or fixed. Ignoring an entry keeps it out of the open count and the email reports without deleting its history."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:355
msgid "The log entry ID."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:375
msgid "Fix a Logged 404"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:376
msgid "Creates a redirect for a logged 404 and links the two, which marks the log entry fixed. The source is taken from the log entry, so only the destination has to be supplied."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:383
msgid "The log entry ID to resolve."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:387
msgid "Destination path or URL."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:391
msgid "ID of an existing page to send visitors to, instead of a URL."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:395
#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:786
msgid "HTTP status code to send. Defaults to 301."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:425
msgid "Get 404 to 301 Settings"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:426
msgid "Returns every plugin setting as a flat map: the site-wide 404 fallback, 404 logging, email notifications and reports, and log trimming."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:439
msgid "Update 404 to 301 Settings"
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:440
msgid "Writes plugin settings from a flat map of the same keys the get ability returns. Only the keys passed in are changed. Unknown keys are ignored, and the Telegram credentials cannot be written here."
msgstr ""

#: app/Abilities/Abilities.php:447
msgid "Flat key => value map of the settings to change."
msgstr ""

